            <ArticleTitle>Considerations in evaluating new antianginal drugs.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>I38-42</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Diseases that cause symptoms incompletely relieved by available modes of treatment stimulate search for new therapies. Chronic disease processes, in which interventions are palliative rather than curative provide a particular challenge in determining the value of therapeutic intervention. Management of patients with angina pectoris is an example of this challenge.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
